-- title:
--   Degree of k₀(̃ j) over k₀(r(̃ j)) equals deg r
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0$ be a field and let $L =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC k₀ 1` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k_0((q))$ generated over $k_0$ by the set $\{x : \exists d \mid 1,\ x = \mathtt{qExpand}\ d\ \tilde j\}$ of divisor expansions at level $1$; here $\tilde j =$ `jqModC k₀` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot (E_4^3\,\eta^{-24})$ with integral coefficients mapped into $k_0$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Let $r \in k_0[X]$ be a polynomial with $0 < \deg r$ (its `natDegree`). Writing $\tilde j$ also for the corresponding element of $L$ (via the membership witness `jqModC_mem_full k₀ 1`), and $r(\tilde j) =$ `aeval` of $r$ at that element, the assertion is that the $k_0$-intermediate field $k_0(r(\tilde j)) \subseteq L$ generated by the single element $r(\tilde j)$ satisfies
--   $$\operatorname{finrank}_{k_0(r(\tilde j))} L = \deg r,$$
--   that is, $[\,k_0(\tilde j) : k_0(r(\tilde j))\,] = \deg r$ as a module rank over the subfield.
--
--   This is the Lüroth-style degree count for a polynomial substitution in a rational function field, transported to the level-one modular function field $k_0(\tilde j) \subseteq k_0((q))$. It is used in the analysis of prolongations of places of $X_0(q)$ over a pencil line, where residue degrees are computed from polynomials such as $X + \bar\mu X^q$ and $X^q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_adjoin_aeval_jqModC.lean

